.TH ME 1 "2026-04-12" "me 0.3.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
me \- a modern, context-aware replacement for whoami
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B me
[\fIOPTIONS\fR]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B me
prints local identity and session context in a compact, human-readable form.
It keeps the spirit of
.BR whoami (1)
while showing useful local details such as user and group IDs, shell, process IDs,
sudo state, SSH session state, local network summary, and project/container context.
.PP
The default output is intended for humans. Use JSON mode for scripts.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B \-\-help
Print help.
.TP
.B \-\-compact
Use compact one-line output.
.TP
.B \-\-json
Emit structured JSON.
.TP
.B \-\-format \fIFORMAT\fR
Select labeled or config-style output. Supported values are
.B labeled
and
.BR config .
.TP
.B \-\-plain
Print plain identity, defaulting to user@host.
.TP
.B \-\-no-color
Disable ANSI color.
.TP
.B \-\-full
Show full multi-line values where the default is condensed.
.TP
.B \-\-watch
Refresh output in place.
.TP
.B \-\-interval \fISECONDS\fR
Set the watch refresh interval in seconds.
.TP
.B \-\-fast
Skip slower context version checks for prompt usage.
.TP
.B \-\-copy [\fIFIELD\fR]
Copy a field to the clipboard, or prompt when omitted.
.TP
.B \-\-field \fIFIELDS\fR
Select fields by name. Multiple fields may be comma-separated.
.TP
.B \-u
Select user.
.TP
.B \-h
Select host.
.TP
.B \-s
Select shell.
.TP
.B \-p
Select pid.
.TP
.B \-P
Select ppid.
.TP
.B \-t
Select tty.
.TP
.B \-g
Select groups.
.TP
.B \-i
Select uid and gid.
.TP
.B \-n
Select network.
.TP
.B \-V, \-\-version
Print version.
.SH EXAMPLES
.TP
.B me
Show the default block output.
.TP
.B me \-\-compact
Show compact one-line output.
.TP
.B me \-\-json
Emit JSON output.
.TP
.B me \-u \-h \-n
Show only user, host, and network fields.
.TP
.B me \-\-watch \-\-interval 2
Refresh output every two seconds.
.SH CONTEXT
.B me
detects a small set of local context signals: SSH sessions, Docker/container
environments, common project types such as Rust, Node, Python, Go, Java,
Ruby, C/C++, PHP, Lua, Swift, R, and C#, and Git branches when the current
directory is inside a Git work tree.
.PP
Context is summarized quietly in the default block output.
.SH NOTES
Because
.B \-h
selects host, help is available as
.BR \-\-help .
